  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Creating a binary with two digests is only returning one digest on GET:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "language": "java"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "echo \"test content\" |\r\ncurl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -XPUT http://localhost:8080/rest/binary_with_digests --data-binary @- -H \"Digest: md5=d6eb32081c822ed572b70567826d9d9d, sha=4fe2b8dd12cd9cd6a413ea960cd8c09c25f19527\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "GET",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "language": "java"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "$ curl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http://localhost:8080/rest/binary_with_digests/fcr:metadata\r\n\r\n<http://localhost:8080/rest/binary_with_digests>\r\n        ...\r\n        premis:hasMessageDigest  <urn:sha1:4fe2b8dd12cd9cd6a413ea960cd8c09c25f19527> ;",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The header file actually has the MD5, SHA1, and SHA512 stored, so its most likely an issue when generating the response:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "language": "java"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "\"digests\":[\"urn:sha1:4fe2b8dd12cd9cd6a413ea960cd8c09c25f19527\",\"urn:md5:d6eb32081c822ed572b70567826d9d9d\",\"urn:sha-512:b22137a0e8969282b85e3f9375448307d14c5aabf41be66c4f6a0323bd03a3935972021e4c34aa30914e37b03c22594fe180eea9790e9ff147016c9dfae39d5a\"]",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Ideally, the GET response would contain all 3 of the digests.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
