  "description": "<p>Creating a binary with two digests is only returning one digest on GET:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\necho <span class=\"code-quote\">\"test content\"</span> |\r\ncurl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -XPUT http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/binary_with_digests --data-binary @- -H <span class=\"code-quote\">\"Digest: md5=d6eb32081c822ed572b70567826d9d9d, sha=4fe2b8dd12cd9cd6a413ea960cd8c09c25f19527\"</span></span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>GET</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n$ curl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/binary_with_digests/fcr:metadata\r\n</span>\r\n&lt;http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/binary_with_digests&gt;\r\n</span>        ...\r\n        premis:hasMessageDigest  &lt;urn:sha1:4fe2b8dd12cd9cd6a413ea960cd8c09c25f19527&gt; ;\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>The header file actually has the MD5, SHA1, and SHA512 stored, so its most likely an issue when generating the response:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n<span class=\"code-quote\">\"digests\"</span>:[<span class=\"code-quote\">\"urn:sha1:4fe2b8dd12cd9cd6a413ea960cd8c09c25f19527\"</span>,<span class=\"code-quote\">\"urn:md5:d6eb32081c822ed572b70567826d9d9d\"</span>,<span class=\"code-quote\">\"urn:sha-512:b22137a0e8969282b85e3f9375448307d14c5aabf41be66c4f6a0323bd03a3935972021e4c34aa30914e37b03c22594fe180eea9790e9ff147016c9dfae39d5a\"</span>]\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>Ideally, the GET response would contain all 3 of the digests.</p>",
